# npm pack reads .npmignore INSTEAD of .gitignore once this file exists, for
# the whole tree (warren-402e). That is the point: src/ui/dist is a gitignored
# build artifact but MUST ship in the published tarball, and gitignore rules
# cannot re-include files under an excluded directory.
#
# Consequence: gitignore exclusions under the package.json "files" whitelist
# no longer apply at pack time. The whitelist is narrow (`src`, minus UI
# sources, plus `src/ui/dist`) and its only gitignored contents live under
# src/ui/, which "files" already excludes. If you add a new gitignored build
# artifact under an included path, add its exclusion HERE so it does not ship.
!dist/
